---
title: Cold Brew
image: https://www.simplyrecipes.com/thmb/GIQGYNbvTns7oqIHgjn15Gqk1-w=/750x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/Simply-Recipes-Cold-Brew-Coffee-LEAD-20-5cb9bb5dd8f44376909a83482e97eb44.jpg
time required: 12 hours
servings: 4
prep time: 5 minutes
---

In a #cold brew maker{}, place your @coffee{1%cup}(coarsely ground) in the brew filter. Insert the brew filter into the carafe.

Slowly pour @cold water{4%cups} over the coffee. Once filled, stir grounds until fully saturated with water. 

Tighten lid and refrigerate for ~{12-15%hours}.

Stir grounds and taste. If flavor seems weak, refrigerate for another ~{12-15%hours}. Just be careful to note over steep. Remove brew filter and grounds whenever satisfied with strength. 

> The important part is to preserve a 1:4 coffee to water ratio, so it's best to determine the capacity of your carafe first, then calculate the proper coffee ground amount.

> You can also prepare this in a mason jar or french press if you don't have a cold brew maker. If using french press, make sure the plunge is pressed down to submerge grounds before storing. For a mason jar, be prepared to strain using filter or cloth.